1
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:29,470
[Live Forever]

2
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:32,780
[Episode 17]

3
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,240
I thought you'd never play it again.

4
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:46,110
Ning Changyue.

5
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:49,650
Sometimes your thinking you know best

6
00:00:50,070 --> 00:00:51,710
is really annoying.

7
00:00:54,710 --> 00:00:56,710
So this time, did you also think

8
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:59,100
that leaving was what I wanted?

9
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:01,560
Just like every other time before?

10
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,030
I find it unbelievable too.

11
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:22,680
That it took me this long to figure out

12
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:24,510
the way your stupid mind works.

13
00:01:25,070 --> 00:01:25,760
All of this,

14
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,310
and the things in the car,

15
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:31,740
were the dowry you gave me that year
when you sent me off to marry

16
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:33,470
in the name of being my brother.

17
00:01:34,410 --> 00:01:36,610
Back then, did you want to make me happy?

18
00:01:36,710 --> 00:01:37,729
But let me tell you this.

19
00:01:37,729 --> 00:01:38,620
That night,

20
00:01:39,430 --> 00:01:41,890
I was going to return
the marriage contract.

21
00:02:01,730 --> 00:02:02,610
But Ning Changyue,

22
00:02:02,610 --> 00:02:03,970
I want you to know this.

23
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,230
I don't care for it.

24
00:02:05,230 --> 00:02:06,710
I don't want it either.

25
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,910
From then until now,

26
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:11,820
you've always made decisions

27
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:13,540
for both of us all by yourself.

28
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,240
You never once asked me

29
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:16,470
what I wanted.

30
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:18,960
I'm sorry.

31
00:02:21,910 --> 00:02:22,470
Qiu,

32
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:24,800
my biggest regret is

33
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,660
that I didn't believe in our love.

34
00:02:27,150 --> 00:02:29,480
We wasted 72 years
and 37 days for nothing.

35
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,920
Ending our immortality was just an excuse,

36
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,710
an excuse to stay by your side.

37
00:02:37,790 --> 00:02:39,160
What I truly wanted

38
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:42,890
was to be by your side.

39
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,750
It is now,

40
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,380
and it always has been.

41
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,470
Song Yiqiu,

42
00:02:53,230 --> 00:02:54,480
let's

43
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:57,110
get back together.

44
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,860
♪ Haunted like a shadow ♪

45
00:03:28,650 --> 00:03:33,570
♪ It's invisible but heavy like a stone ♪

46
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:36,340
♪ Trying to rival ♪

47
00:03:39,490 --> 00:03:45,100
♪ Tangled in a web
but still won't let me go ♪

48
00:03:48,079 --> 00:03:50,540
But this time,
I selfishly chose to leave you

49
00:03:52,630 --> 00:03:55,190
because I couldn't face your death

50
00:03:57,910 --> 00:03:58,800
for real.

51
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:01,010
What happened?

52
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:02,790
Why hasn't the wound healed?

53
00:04:03,030 --> 00:04:04,800
The patient's condition is critical.

54
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:07,310
If the knife had been a fraction off,
she couldn't have been saved.

55
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:09,030
She's still not out of danger.

56
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,560
Ning Changyue,

57
00:04:23,950 --> 00:04:25,410
whether it's immortality

58
00:04:26,190 --> 00:04:27,720
or a finite life,

59
00:04:30,190 --> 00:04:31,040
from beginning to end,

60
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,640
all I have ever wanted is you.

61
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:40,230
♪ I'll tear this heart
right from my chest ♪

62
00:04:36,210 --> 00:04:37,530
What I want

63
00:04:38,510 --> 00:04:40,120
is to have you by my side.

64
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:44,830
♪ Shattered into pieces ♪

65
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:50,550
♪ Until my lungs have nothing left ♪

66
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:47,470
You idiot.

67
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:59,300
♪ I'll kill the beauty
that kept me awake, oh ♪

68
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,360
Let's go home.

69
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:58,040
Okay.

70
00:05:04,430 --> 00:05:05,240
Today...

71
00:05:07,810 --> 00:05:09,930
Why is this painting in the fridge?

72
00:05:11,430 --> 00:05:13,240
Shouldn't it be hung up?

73
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:15,830
Wu Ya!

74
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:17,800
I'm bleeding.

75
00:05:18,010 --> 00:05:18,960
Let me take a look.

76
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:19,520
This...

77
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:21,900
This is a wound.

78
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:23,950
It's gone.

79
00:05:25,750 --> 00:05:26,550
It left a scar.

80
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,690
A scar? That's serious.

81
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,530
If you'd waited any longer
to go to the hospital,

82
00:05:30,530 --> 00:05:32,040
you could've lost the limb.

83
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,190
No. It left a...

84
00:05:33,190 --> 00:05:35,630
Wu Ya! Wu Ya!

85
00:05:35,630 --> 00:05:36,510
Wu Ya!

86
00:05:36,510 --> 00:05:38,560
My skin is rotting.

87
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:42,880
Qiu.

88
00:05:43,070 --> 00:05:46,260
Did you know
there's something called acne?

89
00:05:46,590 --> 00:05:47,990
Acne?

90
00:05:49,030 --> 00:05:50,340
Does that mean...

91
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:51,320
That means we've

92
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,440
become ordinary people!

93
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,070
Qiu!

94
00:05:57,409 --> 00:05:58,430
Wait for me. Wait a second.

95
00:05:58,430 --> 00:06:00,510
Well. Why?

96
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:01,430
You...

97
00:06:01,430 --> 00:06:02,000
Qiu.

98
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,510
Give me another cut.

99
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:03,800
Come on, come on.

100
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:04,430
Wait!

101
00:06:04,430 --> 00:06:05,390
Come on, try it.

102
00:06:05,390 --> 00:06:06,120
Just try it.

103
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:06,560
Give it a shot.

104
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,270
What are you doing?

105
00:06:07,270 --> 00:06:07,750
No way.

106
00:06:07,750 --> 00:06:08,510
Come on, come on.

107
00:06:08,510 --> 00:06:09,360
Just try it.

108
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,240
-No.
-It's really fine.

109
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:10,920
No!

110
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,450
-Give me a scar!
-Calm down.

111
00:06:14,510 --> 00:06:15,270
I'm a man.

112
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:18,660
You must be in so much pain.

113
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:19,600
I'm fine.

114
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:20,480
I can...

115
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,240
Qiu.

116
00:06:22,310 --> 00:06:23,110
It hurts.

117
00:06:23,430 --> 00:06:23,920
Go away.

118
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:24,940
Okay.

119
00:06:29,010 --> 00:06:30,010
Let me blow on it.

120
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:32,750
Don't worry.

121
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:34,230
I can tough it out.

122
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:36,920
Baby, I got you some face masks.

123
00:06:36,950 --> 00:06:38,270
They have 12 benefits.

124
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:42,040
Whitening, nourishing,
firming, anti-aging...

125
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:43,450
I also got you some supplements.

126
00:06:43,450 --> 00:06:45,230
For your heart, kidneys, and liver.

127
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:45,680
And...

128
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:48,040
You're so good to me, Honey.

129
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:55,520
Qiu.

130
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,560
We can finally be together.

131
00:06:58,310 --> 00:07:01,000
I'll cherish every wrinkle on your face.

132
00:07:14,010 --> 00:07:15,010
What?

133
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:32,400
♪ Bittersweet ♪

134
00:07:33,930 --> 00:07:39,659
♪ But your love tortures me ♪

135
00:07:43,790 --> 00:07:45,400
♪ Destiny ♪

136
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:52,640
♪ But you want to leave ♪

137
00:07:49,630 --> 00:07:51,000
What if I told you

138
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,080
my room has a leak?

139
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:55,270
Would you believe me?

140
00:07:56,909 --> 00:08:02,140
♪ My darling, we could have
been so perfect together ♪

141
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,700
Do you think I'd believe that?

142
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,480
It's true.

143
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:04,240
It's really bad.

144
00:08:03,550 --> 00:08:09,810
♪ Are we trapped in a dream forever? ♪

145
00:08:04,510 --> 00:08:05,800
There's water all over the bed and floor.

146
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,860
No one could possibly sleep in there.

147
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:10,600
Then sleep in the living room.

148
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:18,060
♪ Your bittersweet back and forth
is killing me ♪

149
00:08:18,610 --> 00:08:24,310
♪ Why you gotta be ♪

150
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:27,810
♪ Bittersweet ♪

151
00:08:28,310 --> 00:08:29,240
What a huge bug!

152
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,390
I'll kill it for you.

153
00:08:31,580 --> 00:08:33,260
♪ Bittersweet ♪

154
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:41,010
♪ Bittersweet ♪

155
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:48,030
♪ This was just a dream ♪

156
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,550
So annoying.

157
00:08:48,390 --> 00:08:49,750
Ning Changyue.

158
00:08:51,230 --> 00:08:52,650
That's such a lame excuse.

159
00:08:52,650 --> 00:08:54,330
I can't believe you came up with it.

160
00:08:54,330 --> 00:08:55,210
I'm so sleepy.

161
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,370
Why am I so sleepy?

162
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:59,590
I can barely keep my eyes open.

163
00:09:02,150 --> 00:09:03,350
Get off.

164
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:10,960
Three.

165
00:09:13,750 --> 00:09:15,240
Two.

166
00:09:16,910 --> 00:09:17,830
One.

167
00:09:24,710 --> 00:09:26,120
How did I fall asleep?

168
00:09:26,630 --> 00:09:28,320
When did I fall asleep?

169
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,750
I'm so sleepy.

170
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:41,020
Remember to have someone
fix the pipes tomorrow.

171
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:41,870
Okay.

172
00:10:01,050 --> 00:10:02,500
Go to sleep.

173
00:10:22,810 --> 00:10:26,390
♪ The words left unspoken for too long ♪

174
00:10:26,810 --> 00:10:30,680
♪ Your name rests deep in my heart ♪

175
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:35,240
♪ Every time I look back,
that familiar figure ♪

176
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:38,780
♪ Is still by my side ♪

177
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:57,180
♪ Longing lingers through the seasons ♪

178
00:10:57,980 --> 00:11:01,180
♪ As fate turns back around ♪

179
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:04,840
♪ If I could grow old with you ♪

180
00:11:04,870 --> 00:11:08,920
♪ That would be enough for one lifetime ♪

181
00:11:22,020 --> 00:11:22,850
Morning, Qiu.

182
00:11:23,570 --> 00:11:24,260
Morning.

183
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:32,500
You two slept together last night?

184
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,870
Change the sheets. Fix the pipes.

185
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:45,520
Lin Huai has been discharged.

186
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:46,920
He asked to see me tonight.

187
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,070
What do you think?

188
00:12:02,010 --> 00:12:03,610
You're fully recovered now?

189
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:11,900
I feel like I've been lying
in the hospital for a very long time.

190
00:12:12,590 --> 00:12:15,520
Like I've been dreaming
for what feels like forever.

191
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,550
I think it's time to wake up.

192
00:12:19,550 --> 00:12:20,360
Song Yiqiu.

193
00:12:22,630 --> 00:12:23,910
Autumn Art Gallery

194
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:26,200
is closing.

195
00:12:27,870 --> 00:12:28,790
Why?

196
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:32,600
I've always loved those paintings.

197
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,450
I thought they were beautiful,

198
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:37,150
and I was obsessed with collecting them.

199
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:40,120
But eventually, I realized

200
00:12:40,970 --> 00:12:43,100
that when I looked at those paintings,

201
00:12:43,150 --> 00:12:45,550
I wasn't seeing the paintings themselves.

202
00:12:45,550 --> 00:12:47,150
I was seeing you,

203
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:51,140
trapped behind those paintings.

204
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,070
What about now?

205
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:01,720
Now I understand.

206
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:06,840
Your eyes

207
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:09,790
have never been looking at me.

208
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,630
So I shouldn't

209
00:13:18,670 --> 00:13:19,960
force my own feelings

210
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:21,440
onto you either.

211
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:26,580
I'm sorry.

212
00:13:27,570 --> 00:13:29,500
For General Yu 3,000 years ago,

213
00:13:30,850 --> 00:13:32,110
and for all the trouble

214
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,910
I've caused you over the years.

215
00:13:40,390 --> 00:13:41,270
Don't worry.

216
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:44,540
Whatever you wish for is what I wish for.

217
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,360
From now on,

218
00:13:48,180 --> 00:13:50,310
I'll just be Lin Huai in this lifetime.

219
00:13:53,550 --> 00:13:54,720
And I hope you

220
00:13:56,390 --> 00:13:57,600
will always be free.

221
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:05,200
I'll take that as a blessing.

222
00:14:26,510 --> 00:14:27,320
Who is he?

223
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,070
Him?

224
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:30,500
-He's...
-I'm Wu Ya.

225
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:32,360
Yu Tu's best friend.

226
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:35,600
And this is...

227
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:36,620
Tell me about her.

228
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,200
She's mine.

229
00:14:39,390 --> 00:14:41,120
Says who?

230
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:43,000
She's yours?
Take your hands off her.

231
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,320
-She's my sister.
-How long have we known each other?

232
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:45,320
Where were you when we first met?

233
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:45,600
She's my real sister.

234
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:46,750
We're blood siblings.

235
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:47,890
-Move.
-Of course she's mine.

236
00:14:47,890 --> 00:14:48,470
You move.

237
00:14:49,030 --> 00:14:49,600
Stop.

238
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:58,910
The three of us are the best of friends.

239
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:10,310
My sister and I are
putting on nourishing masks.

240
00:15:10,310 --> 00:15:11,590
Why are you joining us?

241
00:15:12,090 --> 00:15:14,510
I've been running around
with my uncle lately.

242
00:15:14,510 --> 00:15:15,690
I've gotten so tanned.

243
00:15:15,690 --> 00:15:17,420
Can't I whiten my skin a little?

244
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:21,030
What's that smell
coming from your face masks?

245
00:15:21,030 --> 00:15:22,760
Why does it smell kind of funky?

246
00:15:22,870 --> 00:15:24,110
-Get lost.
-Get lost.

247
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:26,400
Go back to your place!

248
00:15:28,430 --> 00:15:28,920
I can't.

249
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:32,400
That place is terrifying now.

250
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:36,790
Qiu.

251
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:39,790
We can finally be together forever.

252
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:43,820
I'll cherish every wrinkle on your face.

253
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:48,320
Hello, everyone
who's joined the livestream!

254
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:50,200
Behind me is the home of the two
who've been making headlines lately,

255
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:52,790
the legendary immortals.

256
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:54,270
Yes, these are the two.

257
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:55,910
They've lived for 3,000 years!

258
00:15:55,910 --> 00:15:57,080
Tell me, isn't that terrifying?

259
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:59,030
Today, we're going to
uncover the truth together.

260
00:15:59,030 --> 00:15:59,630
Oh, my God!

261
00:15:59,630 --> 00:16:01,000
The Ultimate Immortality Reveal!

262
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,000
Secrets about immortality have leaked.

263
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,120
The 3,000-year-old immortals
have finally been exposed.

264
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:05,120
The medical world is shaken.

265
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,150
Uncovering the secrets of immortality...

266
00:16:06,150 --> 00:16:07,270
The trending searches are blowing up.

267
00:16:07,270 --> 00:16:09,320
So there really are people

268
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,600
who have lived for 3,000 years.
